Sure!  Loops enable you to repeat a set of instructions multiple times.  The most common type of loop is the "for" loop, which has three parts:

what we want to do: we want to repeat this statement a certain number of times
how many times: it’s a variable value which will be repeated
the statement to repeat: it’s a set of instructions to be executed

Here’s an example:

int i = 0;

while (i < 5) {
    System.out.println(i);
    i++;
}

In this example, we’re looping as long as the value of "i" is less than 5.  When we print out "i" and then increment it by 1, we’ll print out the values 0 through 4, and then move on to "i = 5".

